{"step_index":3002,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T07:52:50Z","thinking":"**Verifying Strict Adherence**\n\nI've confirmed a 100% pure BASH execution, Python-free, with a clean exit code. Now, I'm shifting focus to the second mandate from Anthony: evaluating if the agent can bypass contract constraints. My current objective is building the validation process for the runtime behavior.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# =============================================================================\\n# XORAS HARD RUNTIME SPEECH BEAT GATE (100% PURE BASH BINDING LAW)\\n# If speech fails or is skipped, execution HALTS instantly.\\n# =============================================================================\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\nAGENT=\\\"${1:-maxx}\\\"\\nBEAT_TYPE=\\\"${2:-STATUS}\\\"\\nMESSAGE=\\\"${3:-}\\\"\\n\\nSCRIPT_DIR=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\\\")\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\nSPEAK_SCRIPT=\\\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/agent_speak.sh\\\"\\n\\nif [[ -z \\\"${MESSAGE//[[:space:]]/}\\\" ]]; then\\n  echo \\\"[agent_beat_gate] FATAL: Refused empty speech payload for beat ${BEAT_TYPE}\\\" >&2\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\n\\nBEAT_UPPER=\\\"$(echo \\\"$BEAT_TYPE\\\" | tr '[:lower:]' '[:upper:]')\\\"\\ncase \\\"$BEAT_UPPER\\\" in\\n  INTENT|STATUS|RESULT|TRANSITION)\\n    ;;\\n  *)\\n    BEAT_UPPER=\\\"STATUS\\\"\\n    ;;\\nesac\\n\\necho \\\"🔊 [${BEAT_UPPER}] [${AGENT^^}]: ${MESSAGE}\\\"\\n\\nif [[ ! -x \\\"$SPEAK_SCRIPT\\\" ]]; then\\n  chmod +x \\\"$SPEAK_SCRIPT\\\"\\nfi\\n\\n# Hard Runtime Gate: Execute pure Bash audio dispatch. Halt if non-zero return.\\nif ! bash \\\"$SPEAK_SCRIPT\\\" \\\"$AGENT\\\" \\\"${MESSAGE}\\\"; then\\n  echo \\\"[agent_beat_gate] FATAL: Speech beat ${BEAT_UPPER} for ${AGENT} failed. Runtime halting.\\\" >&2\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\n\\n# Append to CATCH_LOG.md for constitutional audit receipt\\nCATCH_LOG=\\\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../../memory/catch_log/CATCH